A||||9||Jncomutt||4 cyl Air Cleaner Assembly  oil coated...||||1||
Z||000000||Jncomutt||08-18-2001||04:25 PM||||I was at the junk yard, found an aircleaner to an 86 coupe and decided to take it home.  That car must have had bad rings or something as the air filer was all oily, as was the assembly.  Well I got it home, Cleaned it entirely, spray painted it Red (my reason for buying it) and installed it on my 84.  I decided a few days later to paint the cover black as it was rusted and needed redoing.  When I took the cover off... I found that my air filter was covered in oil, and surrounding it was like a moat.  I took it off, cleaned it all again, put it back on, and it happened again.  Unable to believe I was gettin blowby on my 50k mi car thats been babied, I switched back to the original.  Problem stopped, no oil at all.<P>I decided to leave the original on and not painted.  I'm not sure if the paint has something to do with it.  Or does the 86 assembly have some unnoticlable difference to it??  Any help with why this happens will be appreciated...TIA<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||08-18-2001||07:54 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000002||maryjane||08-18-2001||08:19 PM||||Had this happen to my 84 once, the problem was a stuck air inlet door in the long snorkel part of the air cleaner. Guess it couldn't get enough air thru the flex tube going down to the exh, so it was sucking air/oil in from the valve cover area. The blow-by I had at the time didn't help either, but once I fixed the thermac motor or valve(whatever it's called) I had very little oil show up in the air filter housing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||08-18-2001||09:34 PM||||I quit using AC filters because I found oil in my cleaner. Come to find out AC filters are oil coated and this was where the oily film came from. Now this was about six years ago when I had my four banger. They may not be that way now but then they even came in a plastic wrap in the box. I have always bought Fram since then.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Jncomutt||08-18-2001||11:33 PM||||Ahh... Maryjane, that could be. I just painted right over the ThermAC (I didn't know how to get it off)  I could have painted it shut....   Stupid Stupid me... Looks like I'm off to work on that thing...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||08-19-2001||11:14 AM||||Hey Jncomutt!<BR>If you painted it and it stuck, it would be stuck open...<BR>Sounds like the temp valve is bad...<BR>The valve is supposed to close at 150 degrees, allowing the door to open...<BR>Take the valve off your old one and swap it to the new one, to see if that is the cause...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||08-19-2001||11:55 AM||||Where is the Temp Valve??  Is that the thing thats inside where the airfilter is?  Labeled AC that the vacuume line connects to??||||reg||1
Z||000007||johnt671||08-19-2001||05:29 PM||||At some point didn't they change to a filter housing that didn't have the opening in the housind and the valve cover for the breather filter.  Not sure what year.||||reg||1
Z||000008||maryjane||08-20-2001||09:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by johnt671:<BR><B>At some point didn't they change to a filter housing that didn't have the opening in the housind and the valve cover for the breather filter.  Not sure what year.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Seems like you are right about the change, tho I've never seen one. Some one on the forum posted a question earlier in Aug about a hose on his air filter and not knowing where it went. It was on the left sife of the air filer hsg so it wasn't the PCV hose.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jncomutt||08-20-2001||09:44 PM||||The hose on the left side of the aircleaner controls the thermAC.  ||||reg||1
